{"assignees":[{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1OTM5NDIy","login":"Syuizen","name":"Yiran Zhu","databaseId":15939422}],"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNTI0OA==","is_bot":false,"login":"Krastanov","name":"Stefan Krastanov"},"body":"# A reliable idiomatic `networkx` wrapper [$400]\n\nUsing networkx through PythonCall.jl is trivially easy. This bounty is mostly about creating a new NetworkX.jl wrapper (by using PythonCall.jl) that provides quality-of-life improvements, \n\n- [ ] Fast conversion and/or views between Graphs.jl types and the networkx structures\n- [ ] Complete Graph API support for the newly created networkx wrapper types (so that networkx types can be used in all already existing Graph.jl algorithms that do not peek behind the API)\n- [ ] use GraphsInterfaceChecker.jl in the test suite\n- [ ] Dispatch from operations defined in Graphs/GraphsMatching/GraphsOptim to networkx implementation. For instance if there is a pre-existing `Graphs.some_interesting_property(::AbstractGraph)` there should now be a new method defined in NetworkX `some_interesting_property(g::AbstractGraph, ::NXAlgorithm)` that dispatches to the networkx implementation. It should convert the `g` argument to networkx graphs if necessary.\n- [ ] If there is an algorithm defined in networkx that does not exist yet in Graphs.jl, it should be declared in Graphs.jl (just a function with docs but no methods), together with an error hint that NetworkX is necessary. Given the large scope of the library, this can be more of a proof-of-concept setup, documenting how to add everything, but not expecting everything to be added for completing the bounty. \n- [ ] Proper tests and documentation.\n- [ ] PRs on this topic have to be submitted with clean git histories and well compartmentalized for ease of review. \n\n**Required skills**: familiarity with the Graphs.jl API and understanding of the PythonCall package\n\n**Reviewer**: any Graphs.jl member with merge rights\n\n**Duration**: 3 months\n\n#### Payout procedure:\n\nThe Funding for these bounties comes from the National Science Foundation and from the NSF Center for Quantum Networks. The payouts are managed by the NumFOCUS foundation and processed in bulk once every two months. If you live in a country in which NumFOCUS can make payments, you can participate in this bounty program.\n\n[Click here for more details about the bug bounty program.](https://github.com/QuantumSavory/.github/blob/main/BUG_BOUNTIES.md)\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Bug bounty logistic details</strong> (click to expand)</summary>\n\nTo claim exclusive time to work on this bounty either post a comment here or message [skrastanov@umass.edu](mailto:skrastanov@umass.edu) with:\n\n- your name\n- github username\n- **(optional)** a brief list of previous pertinent projects you have engaged in\n\nIf you want to, you can work on this project without making a claim, however claims are encouraged to give you and other contributors peace of mind. Whoever has made a claim takes precedence when solutions are considered.\n\nYou can always propose your own funded project, if you would like to contribute something of value that is not yet covered by an official bounty.\n</details>\n","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh868Fc6j","author":{"login":"Syuizen"},"authorAssociation":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"Hey @Krastanov , \n\nI'm interested in taking this up. The main reason is that I've coded extensively in Python for past 8 years and my work mostly deals with graph library, and arguably, `NetworkX.py` has most extensive methods implemented, that's why I often use `NetworkX.py` to do prototype. Well, not surprisingly, I was struggling with the long runtime when working on large-scale graphs.\n\nThis is the exact reason which brings me into `Graphs.jl`. I wanted to say thanks you so much for building such high performance graph library, and keep maintaining it. For this project, I did see the value of using wrapper to consume the extensive methods available from `NetworkX`. It also opens many gates for future refactoring / Julia-native implementation of these methods.\n\nLet's talk a bit about my background. As for Julia, I has just joined this loving community for about 6 months, and happy to get my very first [Julia CR accepted in `Graphs.jl`](https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/pull/415). I won't claim myself as expert, but I do have the confidence to get this job done.\n\nI'd hope to take this as a chance to better understand the interactions between Julia and Python, and this is the major (sole) motivation for me to do this bounty.\n\n","createdAt":"2025-08-05T14:49:59Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449#issuecomment-3155545763","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh868y7-6","author":{"login":"Krastanov"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"Thanks folks for expressing interest in the bounty! Just a quick correction: while I do some minor maintenance work here, this library was built by others (mostly `simonschoelly` and `gdalle` in the last few years, and other significant contributors earlier on)\n\nLet's start with assigning this to @iamrajiv simply because they expressed interest first. However, given that there are multiple volunteers that want to engage with this, I would ask you @iamrajiv to be a bit more proactive in showing progress -- e.g. by submitting a rough plan in the next few days and some initial prototype withing a couple of weeks. This is of course mostly volunteer work so it would be inappropriate of me to make significant demands (the bounty is pretty small for the actual contribution given back to the community), but I have to put in some work to protect the ecosystem from spam submissions generated with an LLM. In particular, I have had to cancel bounties in the last few months when it turns out that a contributor has misrepresented their knowledge of Julia, e.g. by proposing a nonsensical initial plan or by not knowing how to set up a simple empty package. I never assume this at the start, but it is something I have to proactively guard against, hence this long list of caveats and warnings here.\n\n@Syuizen , I would be eager to help onboard you on any of the other bounties or to increase the total award for this bounty so that it can be split with @iamrajiv (after we hear his initial plan and deciding how the work can be split).\n\nBoth of you, feel free to message me at skrastanov@umass.edu if you want more privacy in how you discuss your plans.","createdAt":"2025-08-08T10:54:13Z","includesCreatedEdit":true,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449#issuecomment-3167469498","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh8693EMz","author":{"login":"Krastanov"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"Hi, @iamrajiv ! Could you confirm you are looking into this bounty? Please let us know how you want to proceed with the bounty, etc. Check out the questions and suggestions from the previous comment.","createdAt":"2025-08-13T19:38:15Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":true,"minimizedReason":"outdated","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449#issuecomment-3185328947","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh86-Ygjc","author":{"login":"Krastanov"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"The bounty is open again as iamrajiv did not respond whether they want to engage with the bounty. @Syuizen are you interesting in pursuing it?","createdAt":"2025-08-17T03:23:46Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449#issuecomment-3194095836","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh86-olXe","author":{"login":"Syuizen"},"authorAssociation":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"@Krastanov Yes! definitely interested. May I know how I could better start on this project?","createdAt":"2025-08-18T20:23:49Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[{"content":"HEART","users":{"totalCount":1}}],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449#issuecomment-3198309854","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh86-opau","author":{"login":"Krastanov"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"I would suggest first setting up a package that uses PythonCall to import networkx of a particular version. Check out PyQDecoders.jl for a simple example. Then set up a struct that wraps around the networkx struct and follows the Graphs.jl API as verified by GraphInterfaceChecker. Check out NautyGraphs.jl for an example of such set of tests. From there we can build out the rest relatively easily. Check out the Graphs.jl repository for how to structure the CI (in `.github`).","createdAt":"2025-08-18T20:30:18Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[{"content":"THUMBS_UP","users":{"totalCount":1}}],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449#issuecomment-3198326446","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh86-oqbR","author":{"login":"Krastanov"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"You should also have constructors `Graph(::NetworkXGraph)` and `NetworkXGraph(::Graph)`.","createdAt":"2025-08-18T20:31:50Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449#issuecomment-3198330577","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh86-pHqa","author":{"login":"Syuizen"},"authorAssociation":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"Sounds good! I have never done CI before, and using PythonCall is also new to me.\n\nMy plan is to start with a new repo to have the two constructors implemented as you mentioned. Then I will add CI.\n\nETA will be 1 week for the new repo + 2 constructors and another week for CI.","createdAt":"2025-08-18T21:15:54Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[{"content":"HEART","users":{"totalCount":1}}],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449#issuecomment-3198450330","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh87DtvCE","author":{"login":"Krastanov"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"@Syuizen , how is this going? Is there anything I can help with?","createdAt":"2025-09-12T03:46:30Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449#issuecomment-3283546244","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh87EGQ_U","author":{"login":"Syuizen"},"authorAssociation":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"Hi @Krastanov , all good. Sorry for being silent for a while. Was busy with a conference travel. I should share the repo by end of this week.","createdAt":"2025-09-14T22:29:14Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449#issuecomment-3289976788","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh87F-dGE","author":{"login":"Syuizen"},"authorAssociation":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"@Krastanov I keep my updates on a toy repo first [GraphsNxExample.jl](https://github.com/Syuizen/GraphsNxExample.jl)\n\nI'm exploring the most efficient way of converting networkX graphs back into Graphs.jl. It was a surprise to me that using sparse matrix is not faster than simply loop over all edges.\n\nI will continue working on that repo and keep posts here whenever I have updates. In the meantime, please let me know if you (or anyone reading this thread) have any comments!","createdAt":"2025-09-22T21:03:52Z","includesCreatedEdit":true,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449#issuecomment-3321483652","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh87F_UtF","author":{"login":"Krastanov"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"Thanks for the heads up! A few misc comments:\n\n- setting it up as a package can help with a lot of chores (although that setup is itself a chore). Check out VNGraphs/LemonGraphs/IGraphs for an example package structure or just use PackageTemplates. In particular, bringing over the .github folder and test folder can speed up a lot of your work\n- depending on exactly how the sparse matrix is stored, it might be less efficient for representing a graph -- there is a great variety in how this can be set up\n- check out PyQDecoders for a simple example of how to import python packages in a julia library -- the import might interact weirdly with pre-compilation, so it can be a pain to set it up properly\n- you can go ahead and use a more final name -- name changes are easy before the package gets registered","createdAt":"2025-09-22T22:34:08Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449#issuecomment-3321711429","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh87oKEQ9","author":{"login":"zhanglin2603"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"Hi team, I read through JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl#449 and I can own this (listed bounty: $400).\n- My read: this is primarily a UI/UX task tied to \"A reliable idiomatic wrapper for networkx [$400]\".\n- I will focus on these issue-specific points first: reliable, idiomatic, wrapper.\n- First I will reproduce and confirm expected behavior for the UI/UX path.\n- Then I will implement the fix with targeted tests and keep scope tight (high confidence).\n- I will share a working PR update fast (24h for scoped implementation plan, 48h+ for full patch and validation) with verification notes.\nIf this approach works for you, I can start now.\n","createdAt":"2026-02-13T05:17:55Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":true,"minimizedReason":"spam","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449#issuecomment-3894953021","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh87oKoBK","author":{"login":"zhanglin2603"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"Thanks for the feedback. You are right, I will keep future updates specific to this issue and avoid template-style replies.","createdAt":"2026-02-13T06:07:19Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":true,"minimizedReason":"spam","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449#issuecomment-3895099466","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh87oLkuX","author":{"login":"nenadilic84"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"I've started working on this bounty. Initial implementation is at https://github.com/nenadilic84/NetworkX.jl\n\n**Current status (106 tests passing):**\n\n### Completed checklist items:\n- [x] Fast conversion between Graphs.jl types and networkx structures (`NXGraph(::SimpleGraph)` and `SimpleGraph(::NXGraph)`, same for directed)\n- [x] Complete Graph API support for `NXGraph` and `NXDiGraph` types (nv, ne, vertices, edges, has_vertex, has_edge, outneighbors, inneighbors, add_edge!, rem_edge!, add_vertex!, rem_vertex!, copy, zero, eltype, edgetype, is_directed)\n- [x] GraphsInterfaceChecker test written (pending registry availability for CI)\n- [x] `NXAlgorithm` dispatch type for operations: `is_connected`, `connected_components`, `diameter`, `radius`, `density`, `pagerank`, `betweenness_centrality`, `closeness_centrality`\n- [x] New function `local_clustering_coefficient` declared as proof-of-concept for algorithms only available in networkx (with error hint when NetworkX.jl not loaded)\n- [x] Proper tests (106 passing) and documentation\n\n### Implementation details:\n- Uses PythonCall.jl + CondaPkg.jl for seamless Python interop\n- Automatically installs networkx, numpy, scipy via Conda\n- 1-based vertex indexing throughout for Graphs.jl compatibility\n- Both undirected (`NXGraph`) and directed (`NXDiGraph`) supported\n\nHappy to receive feedback on what additional algorithms or features should be prioritized. The repo is ready for transfer to JuliaGraphs once reviewed.","createdAt":"2026-02-13T07:27:23Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":true,"minimizedReason":"outdated","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449#issuecomment-3895348119","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh87oMC-z","author":{"login":"nenadilic84"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"**CI Update**: All tests now pass on CI across all 3 platforms:\n- Ubuntu (x64) ✅\n- Windows (x64) ✅\n- macOS (aarch64) ✅\n\nBadge: https://github.com/nenadilic84/NetworkX.jl/actions/workflows/ci.yml\n\nThe package is ready for review. Happy to move it under the JuliaGraphs org or submit a PR to an existing repo structure whenever the maintainers prefer.","createdAt":"2026-02-13T07:59:08Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":true,"minimizedReason":"outdated","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449#issuecomment-3895472051","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh87oMdgu","author":{"login":"lmee"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"I read through the full thread for \"A reliable idiomatic wrapper for networkx [$400]\" including all comments. The core problem appears to be: A reliable idiomatic wrapper [$400]. My root-cause hypothesis is an FFI boundary mismatch (types/ownership/error handling) between wrapper code and native APIs. A key detail from the discussion is: \"I would suggest first setting up a package that uses PythonCall to import networkx of a particular version. Check out PyQDecoders.jl for a simple example. Then set up a struct that.\" My plan is to define a minimal wrapper surface first, align types and ownership semantics with the native API, then add deterministic tests for correctness, memory safety, and failure-path behavior. I can start now and keep updates focused on evidence and validation. Best, Jerry Li","createdAt":"2026-02-13T08:29:02Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":true,"minimizedReason":"spam","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449#issuecomment-3895580718","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh87pB0IE","author":{"login":"energypantry"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"Hi @Krastanov, I read this thread fully, including the current implementation progress already shared by others.\n\nIf additional contributors are still welcome, I can focus on a complementary, reviewable slice:\n- conversion-path hardening between `Graphs.jl` and NetworkX wrappers,\n- edge-case tests and docs around algorithm dispatch,\n- small PRs with clear boundaries to reduce review load.\n\nIf this bounty is still open for parallel contribution, I can start immediately and post the first scoped PR update in ~48 hours.\n","createdAt":"2026-02-16T16:57:30Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":true,"minimizedReason":"spam","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449#issuecomment-3909566980","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh88AAAABAel-4w","author":{"login":"AJ0070"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"@Krastanov I will simultaneously start working on this because reviews might take time due to time zone difference and maintainer  limitations. I will start by creating NetworkX.jl under my account and later I will transfer the ownership to JuliaGraphs if that sounds fine or would you suggest making extension instead of creating a separate repo?","createdAt":"2026-04-27T12:43:00Z","includesCreatedEdit":true,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449#issuecomment-4327046883","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh88AAAABAfC5Ow","author":{"login":"Krastanov"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"Thanks, you are welcome to, but I can not reserve two bounties for you -- if someone else starts working on this while we are still reviewing your other contribution, that is fair game. Same if some of the non-spam previous attempts become revived. This constraint is so that we can prevent \"cookie licking\".\n\n","createdAt":"2026-04-27T13:51:57Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449#issuecomment-4327520571","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh88AAAABAfEH7w","author":{"login":"AJ0070"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"@Krastanov that sounds fair. What do you think about the approach I proposed?","createdAt":"2026-04-27T13:54:41Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449#issuecomment-4327540719","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh88AAAABAfFsUA","author":{"login":"Krastanov"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"Starting under your account makes perfect sense. I would suggest starting with something that uses PythonCall (not PyCall) and first just focus on passing GraphsInterfaceChecker with just the graph constructors and basic API (no algorithms or any interesting features). Having also a few tests that things do not break if multiple threads are working on different graphs would be important -- if you are not careful with the GIL, PythonCall might crash.","createdAt":"2026-04-27T13:58:12Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[{"content":"THUMBS_UP","users":{"totalCount":1}}],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449#issuecomment-4327566416","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh88AAAABAlg2mg","author":{"login":"AJ0070"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"@Krastanov, here is the first draft: [link](https://github.com/AJ0070/NetworkX.jl) I can also add a lightweight CI setup for a single Ubuntu LTS version, so you won’t need to run tests locally.","createdAt":"2026-04-28T10:14:50Z","includesCreatedEdit":true,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449#issuecomment-4334302874","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh88AAAABAnTULg","author":{"login":"Krastanov"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"The following, taken from your link, can be done a bit more idiomatically:\n\n```\ng = path_graph(5)\n\n# Convert Graphs.jl -> Python networkx\npyg = networkx_graph(g)\n\n# Wrap networkx -> Graphs.jl compatible graph\ngw = wrap_networkx(pyg)\n```\n\nInstead of `wrap_networkx`, I believe you can just directly use the constructor for your new wrapper type. Check IGraphs.jl for some style suggestions. I think it would make most sense to have one namespace for the direct access to python's networkx and then the main namespace be dedicated to the julia wrapper tooling following the Graphs.jl API.\n\nAlso, you should have networkx autoinstall -- currently our tests require manual installation of networkx. Check how this is done in things like PyQDecoders.jl. Read through the documentaion of PythonCall.jl and CondaPkg.jl.","createdAt":"2026-04-28T14:28:15Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[{"content":"THUMBS_UP","users":{"totalCount":1}}],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449#issuecomment-4336178222","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh88AAAABAne-kw","author":{"login":"AJ0070"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"I'll do the suggested changes thank you for the guidance.","createdAt":"2026-04-28T14:45:47Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449#issuecomment-4336369299","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh88AAAABArkeJg","author":{"login":"AJ0070"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"@Krastanov I have made an attempt to modify the package based on your feedback. Please let me know your thoughts.","createdAt":"2026-04-29T03:41:39Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449#issuecomment-4340653606","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh88AAAABArl8yQ","author":{"login":"Krastanov"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"Looks good. I would suggest renaming it to NetworkXGraphs.jl to convey that it is meant to follow the Graphs.jl API, then moving it to the JuliaGraphs github organization, then continuing further work through PRs, not through direct pushes to master, so that it is easy to review each next step (in particular, making it easy to review by having separate small PRs each touching a single topic).","createdAt":"2026-04-29T03:50:30Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449#issuecomment-4340677833","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh88AAAABArmcbw","author":{"login":"AJ0070"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"doing it ASAP!","createdAt":"2026-04-29T03:53:08Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449#issuecomment-4340685935","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh88AAAABAro17w","author":{"login":"AJ0070"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"<img width=\"855\" height=\"119\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/81db19cb-9daf-49f5-a187-7cb9b7f57945\" />\n\n@Krastanov I will require ability to create repo in JuliaGraphs.","createdAt":"2026-04-29T04:06:53Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449#issuecomment-4340725231","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh88AAAABArpjHw","author":{"login":"AJ0070"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"<img width=\"722\" height=\"75\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/645067e0-e5a6-4872-928a-e1f72fbaae79\" />\n\nEdit: It has been transferred successfully! ","createdAt":"2026-04-29T04:10:55Z","includesCreatedEdit":true,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449#issuecomment-4340736799","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh88AAAABArqM0A","author":{"login":"AJ0070"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"@Krastanov now what should I focus on?","createdAt":"2026-04-29T04:14:23Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449#issuecomment-4340747472","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh88AAAABAruEhw","author":{"login":"Krastanov"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"Just go one by one through the requirements for this bounty. I would suggest minimal PRs -- they would be much easier to review. Previous comments in this thread have some more detailed suggestions. Of note, some PRs probably will not get reviewers very quickly, so be patient and send occasional reminders about reviews.","createdAt":"2026-04-29T04:33:28Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[{"content":"THUMBS_UP","users":{"totalCount":1}}],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449#issuecomment-4340810887","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOGM0Nh88AAAABA2xWUg","author":{"login":"AJ0070"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"@Krastanov I’m extremely sorry, I mistakenly pushed the changes you requested in my previous PR directly to the main branch of the repo. My `git remote -v origin` was pointing to my fork, and I’m not sure how that happened. I’ve verified that no tests are failing and have enabled branch protection. I’ll make sure this doesn’t happen again.\n","createdAt":"2026-04-30T12:22:37Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[{"content":"THUMBS_UP","users":{"totalCount":1}}],"url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449#issuecomment-4352398930","viewerDidAuthor":false}],"createdAt":"2025-07-24T19:45:53Z","labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDOGM0Nh88AAAABvk05_A","name":"bounty","description":"There is an award for solving this issue.","color":"A6D60A"},{"id":"LA_kwDOGM0Nh88AAAACGFk98w","name":"bounty:400","description":"","color":"aaaaaa"}],"state":"OPEN","title":"A reliable idiomatic wrapper for networkx [$400]","updatedAt":"2026-04-30T12:22:37Z","url":"https://github.com/JuliaGraphs/Graphs.jl/issues/449"}
